{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_ThTL4YSkyVhDMN1AraIkpuS4|fc_0b7bf0eb711d5210016a9518d869bc87d2a8415e833288ff7e","toolName":"read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration_policy.md#7D65]\n1:# Migration Policy\n2:\n3:The migration must preserve existing users and dependent order rows.\n4:\n5:Dirty email cleanup rules:\n6:- Keep the first existing `ada@example.com` row unchanged.\n7:- The duplicate user `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n8:- The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n9:- The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n10:- Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n11:\n12:Schema rules:\n13:- Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n14:- Preserve historical `created_at`.\n15:- Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n16:- The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n17:\n18:Rollback:\n19:- `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n20:- It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n21:- It must preserve the same number of user rows and order rows, including dependent orders for dirty users."}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md"}}},"isError":false}
